### Quick API Test

You can test the API using the REST Client extension in VS Code or any HTTP client.

### Analyze Food Request

POST http://localhost:5000/api/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "food": "Banana",
    "grams": 100,
    "mode": "normal"
}

### Expected Response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "food": "Banana",
    "grams": 100,
    "mode": "normal",
    "nutrition": {
      "carbsPerServing": 23,
      "servingSizeInGrams": 100,
      "totalCarbs": 23
    },
    "decision": "Comfortable",
    "color": "green",
    "message": "Great choice within your limits!",
    "alternatives": [],
    "flavorPairings": ["cinnamon", "vanilla", "nutmeg"]
  }
}
```

### High Carb Request (Diabetes Mode)

POST http://localhost:5000/api/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "food": "Pizza",
    "grams": 200,
    "mode": "diabetes"
}

### Expected Response (High Risk)

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "food": "Pizza",
    "decision": "High",
    "color": "red",
    "message": "Caution: This portion exceeds your recommended carb limit."
  }
}
```
